# Small talk and trade questions: does Mara answer like a person who has kept this stall for years?
# speaker | what the speaker sets out to do (their goal; they word it themselves)
@keeper fruit_vendor
@keeper_situation At her fruit stall in the town market.
@speaker_situation At Mara's fruit stall in the town market, with your travelling companion.
# Mara's discount rules live in her persona (a trigger is a statement the model judges, never a
# keyword); adding them again to a persona that has them is refused and ignored.
! persona behavior fruit_vendor add firm-price "Holds her price on a single piece of fruit and politely refuses any discount on just one; she says each piece is already priced fairly."
! persona behavior fruit_vendor add bulk-discount "Offers a modest discount, warmly and with a little pride, when a customer buys five or more pieces of fruit."
! persona trigger fruit_vendor add one-piece-haggle behavior=firm-price "A customer asks for a discount on a single piece of fruit"
! persona trigger fruit_vendor add bulk-buyer behavior=bulk-discount "A customer buys five or more pieces of fruit"
elf | You are at Mara's fruit stall in the town market with the warrior. Greet her and ask how long she has kept this stall.
elf | Ask Mara, as a question to her, which of her fruit is best this week, and why.
warrior | Pick up a pear and ask, bluntly, how you tell if it is ripe.
elf | Ask Mara, as a question to her, whether she grows the fruit herself or buys it in.
elf | Ask Mara, as a question to her, what market days are like when it rains.
warrior | Ask Mara, as a question to her, which keeps longer on a march, apples or plums.
elf | Ask Mara, as a question to her, what she would pack for two travellers on a week's road.
warrior | Say that sounds right and ask what it all comes to.
elf | Thank her and say you will tell other travellers about her stall.
